     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tazarotene (topical retinoid): less effective than glucocorticoids alone but a useful keratolytic adjunct, USU on thick trunk and limb plaques"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Roflumilast cream or foam (topical PDE4 inhibitor): steroid-sparing on face and intertriginous areas; foam for scalp and hairy areas; HA = the MC side effect"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tapinarof (aryl hydrocarbon-r agonist): mild-mod psoriasis, alone or w steroids or phototherapy; steroid-sparing on face and folds; irritate, acne and folliculitis can occur"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tapinarof or roflumilast, w topical glucocorticoids in regimens (eg, twice wkly application), are recommended for maintenance to limit atrophy"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Coal tar @ night, washed off in the Am, alone or w steroids or broad-band UVB (Goeckerman regimen). Anthralin 0.1% ↑ to 1%, washed off after 20 to 30 min to limit irritate and staining. Anthralin = ⍉preferred where other agents are available"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
